 previous Ten Shadows user was known to have tamed it before the events shown in the story.",
            "Its ability to adapt to phenomena turns the taming ritual into a race to destroy it before it develops an effective response to the user's attacks."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Domain potential",
          paragraphs: [
            "Chimera Shadow Garden floods the environment with the user's shadow medium, multiplying summon angles, clones, storage, movement, and surprise attacks. Megumi's shown version is incomplete and lacks a completed barrier and sure-hit.",
            "Even incomplete, the domain demonstrates why Ten Shadows is valued so highly: it transforms the battlefield itself into the technique's ideal medium."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Common misconceptions",
          bullets: [
            "A shikigami appearing in a ritual does not mean it has been tamed.",
            "Outside help invalidates the ritual for gaining control.",
            "Destroyed shikigami do not all follow a completely unrestricted inheritance system.",
            "Ten Shadows includes shadow manipulation and storage, not only animal summons."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },

    "mahoraga": {
      verified: true,
      source: "Eight-Handled_Sword_Divergent_Sila_Divine_General_Mahoraga",
      sections: [
        {
          title: "The adaptation process",
          paragraphs: [
            "Mahoraga's wheel represents adaptation to phenomena. After it experiences an attack or effect, the wheel turns as the adaptation progresses. Once adapted, Mahoraga develops a response that can resist, recover from, counter, or bypass that phenomenon depending on what it encountered.",
            "Adaptation is not necessarily instantaneous after the first touch. The required exposure and number of turns vary, which creates a window in which an opponent can destroy Mahoraga before the process finishes."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Why overwhelming it quickly matters",
          paragraphs: [
            "Repeating the same attack gives Mahoraga more information and time to complete an answer. A fighter therefore needs enough destructive power to eliminate it before adaptation or must switch to a fundamentally different phenomenon that the wheel has not solved.",
            "Once adaptation is complete, simply increasing the amount of the same ineffective attack may not be enough. The exact response depends on the phenomenon rather than on a generic increase to all defenses."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Sword of Extermination",
          paragraphs: [
            "Mahoraga carries the Sword of Extermination, which is enveloped in positive energy. That makes it especially lethal to cursed spirits, whose bodies are composed of cursed energy.",
            "Mahoraga can also alter how it applies its attacks as adaptation develops, showing that the wheel can produce offensive solutions rather than only defensive resistance."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "The taming ritual",
          paragraphs: [
            "Mahoraga belongs to the Ten Shadows Technique and must be defeated in a valid solo exorcism ritual before the user can command it. Summoning it as an untamed last resort creates a ritual that includes the chosen targets.",
            "If an outsider defeats Mahoraga, the ritual ends but the Ten Shadows user does not gain control. This is why Megumi's emergency summon in Shibuya is not a successful taming."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Common misconceptions",
          bullets: [
            "Mahoraga does not begin a fight already immune to everything.",
            "The wheel adapts to specific phenomena, not automatically to the opponent as an entire person.",
            "Adaptation can create a counter or bypass, not merely higher durability.",
            "Defeating an untamed Mahoraga from outside the ritual does not tame it for the technique's user."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Later manga significance",
          spoiler: "manga",
          paragraphs: [
            "Later manga material demonstrates that Mahoraga's adaptation can continue beyond an initial solution and produce alternative methods of overcoming the same phenomenon. This becomes essential to understanding its role in the battle involving Infinity."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },

    "malevolent-shrine": {
      verified: true,
      source: "Malevolent_Shrine",
      sections: [
        {
          title: "An open domain",
          paragraphs: [
            "Malevolent Shrine manifests Sukuna's domain directly into real space without sealing the target inside a conventional closed barrier. The series compares this to painting on the air rather than on a canvas and treats it as an almost divine barrier feat.",
            "Because the domain leaves an escape route, a binding vow grants it an enormous effective range. Sukuna can adjust that range according to the situation, up to roughly 200 meters when using the full area shown in Shibuya."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "The sure-hit slashes",
          bullets: [
            "Cleave adjusts to targets with cursed energy and is used to cut living or reinforced targets according to their toughness and energy.",
            "Dismantle is applied broadly to objects and the surrounding environment.",
            "The attacks continue relentlessly throughout the domain's effective area rather than arriving as a single slash."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Why the open structure matters in a clash",
          paragraphs: [
            "A conventional domain's barrier is normally strongest against escape from inside and more vulnerable to outside attacks. Malevolent Shrine can occupy the same real space while its slashes strike the exterior shell of the opponent's closed domain.",
            "That creates a structural advantage that is separate from the strength of Sukuna's sure-hit itself. Domain clashes involving Malevolent Shrine therefore depend on both refinement and barrier geometry."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Shibuya use",
          paragraphs: [
            "Sukuna deliberately reduced the maximum radius in Shibuya to avoid catching Megumi in the attack. Even with the reduced area, the domain continuously dismantled people, curses, and structures within range.",
            "The aftermath illustrates the danger of an open domain in a populated city: there is no protective shell containing the destruction."
          ]
        },
        {
          title: "Common misconceptions",
          bullets: [
            "An open domain is still a Domain Expansion; it is not a separate technique category.",
            "The visible shrine is the domain's manifested centerpiece, not a normal building that can simply be destroyed t